-**Note (2026-07-18) — `process-all-pipeline.mjs` now also runs on a schedule.** `com.mitchell.career-ops.daily-triage-queue.plist` runs a single 10:30 PT job that first re-scrapes LinkedIn saved-jobs (an idempotent same-day retry of the 07:15 primary run) and then runs process-all in the SAME sequential process — one job, not two separate plists, so the retry-scrape append can never race the triage's `data/pipeline.md` read/modify/write. That gets saved-jobs / email / HN intake into the dashboard queue without a manual click — closing the gap where scraped jobs piled up un-triaged in `data/pipeline.md`. The per-run triage cap was removed on 2026-07-19 (Mitchell's call), so the scheduled run triages + evals all pending items each day and his LinkedIn saves are never deferred behind other intake by a daily limit; spend is now bounded only by the `MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD` guard inside batch-runner. The former "manual trigger is the safety gate" rationale is superseded: apply-pack pregen + polish (the runaway-cost phases) were removed from Process All on 2026-05-27, so a scheduled run can never auto-build packs or submit — it only triages, evals, and rebuilds the queue. The manual dashboard 🚀 Process All button stays uncapped (cost-confirmation contract). Ships loaded-but-disabled; enable with `launchctl enable gui/$UID/com.mitchell.career-ops.daily-triage-queue`.
-
-**Note (2026-07-19) — LinkedIn auto-unsave is scheduled but ships DOUBLE-DISABLED.** `com.mitchell.career-ops.unsave-processed-linkedin-jobs.plist` runs `scripts/unsave-processed-linkedin-jobs.mjs --apply --scheduled` (via `launchd-wrapper.mjs`) at 12:00 PT — deliberately ~90 min after the 10:30 daily-triage-queue, which writes the `data/linkedin-saved-origin.json` origin ledger and advances `data/applications.md` rows, the two inputs this job intersects to pick its un-save targets (firing before triage finishes would act on a stale set). Unlike the read-only 07:15 saved-jobs SCRAPE (`scan-linkedin-saved-jobs`), this is an **external WRITE** — it clicks the bookmark toggle on linkedin.com to un-save — so it ships behind TWO hand-lifted gates: `Disabled=true` in the plist AND the `LINKEDIN_AUTOUNSAVE_ENABLED` kill switch (the `--scheduled` flag makes the script a 0-exit no-op unless that env var is exactly `true`; the plist deliberately does NOT set it). Only fully-processed jobs are ever candidates; rate-limited, hard per-run cap (`LINKEDIN_AUTOUNSAVE_MAX_PER_RUN`, default 10), every decision appended to `data/linkedin-autounsave-ledger.jsonl`. Enable ONLY after live-fire-verifying the un-save toggle selector (LinkedIn obfuscates + rotates class names): `--probe` (connects, no clicks) → one careful `--apply` → set `LINKEDIN_AUTOUNSAVE_ENABLED=true` in `.env` → `launchctl enable gui/$UID/com.mitchell.career-ops.unsave-processed-linkedin-jobs`. Env-var reference: `docs/reference/env-vars.md`.
+**Note (2026-07-18) — `process-all-pipeline.mjs` now also runs on a schedule.** `com.mitchell.career-ops.daily-triage-queue.plist` runs a single 10:30 PT job that first re-scrapes LinkedIn saved-jobs (an idempotent same-day retry of the 07:15 primary run) and then runs process-all in the SAME sequential process — one job, not two separate plists, so the retry-scrape append can never race the triage's `data/pipeline.md` read/modify/write. That gets saved-jobs / email / HN intake into the dashboard queue without a manual click — closing the gap where scraped jobs piled up un-triaged in `data/pipeline.md`. The scheduled run is cost-capped by `PROCESS_ALL_TRIAGE_LIMIT` (set to 50 in the plist env; caps both triage `--limit` and `--daily-limit`) plus the `MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD` guard inside batch-runner. The former "manual trigger is the safety gate" rationale is superseded: apply-pack pregen + polish (the runaway-cost phases) were removed from Process All on 2026-05-27, so a scheduled run can never auto-build packs or submit — it only triages, evals, and rebuilds the queue. The manual dashboard 🚀 Process All button stays uncapped (cost-confirmation contract). Ships loaded-but-disabled; enable with `launchctl enable gui/$UID/com.mitchell.career-ops.daily-triage-queue`.
 
